.TH "PB-SERVICE-STOP" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-service-stop - Stop Paperboat daemon current-user service


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb service stop [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Stop Paperboat daemon current-user service

.PP
Stop the supervised current-user daemon. Local forwarding and incoming connectivity owned by that process stop until it is started again.

.PP
Service commands manage the current user's background Paperboat daemon through the host operating system. The service runs pb daemon; it is not a separate Paperboat binary. Use status to inspect the supervised process and restart after a local configuration change.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for stop

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-service(1)\fP
